{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underprediction: when the last 10–15 days show a persistent rise (higher highs / higher lows), add a positive level shift to the whole path; the model is systematically too low in bull regimes.",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: errors grow with forecast horizon (small at days 1–3, large by days 7–30). Apply an increasing uplift with lead time (e.g., ramping adjustment rather than a flat offset).",
    "Trend/acceleration lag: the forecast reacts too slowly to rapid repricing (breakouts). If recent slope is steep (e.g., 5-day change > ~+3 to +5), increase near-term slope (not just level) to match acceleration.",
    "Volatility compression: forecast range is too narrow versus realized moves. Inflate forecast volatility/step size during momentum regimes (allow larger daily increments), especially after a breakout.",
    "Late-horizon mean-reversion artifact: the model tends to drift back toward ~69–72 even when the realized market continues trending higher. Reduce/disable mean-reversion pull when trend strength is high (e.g., price above rising MA and MA slope positive)."
  ]
}
